From cdce07b71f1c37dceeb456f2292b5bf48d7d09d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:05:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun6i: exper-t8e: Enable cpufreq with the stock A31
 OPP table

The board file deleted cpu-supply and operating-points from cpu0, which kept
cpufreq-dt from binding (and left "OPP table can't be empty" in the log).
Remove that block so the OPP table of sun6i-a31.dtsi (480/720/864/1008 MHz at
1.0/1.1/1.2/1.2 V) and cpu-supply = <&reg_dcdc3> from the reference-design
tablet include are used.

This depends on the previous commit (settle time for the PLL-CPU): without it
the first frequency change hangs the system. With both, the schedutil governor
moves between all four OPPs on the tablet; stress tests of a few minutes showed
no hang. A single "Runtime PM usage count underflow" panic in sugov on an older
kernel build was not reproduced on the later builds and its cause is unknown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
index 51b4d5e23..6f2366ebf 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
@@ -39,14 +39,6 @@ uart0_ph_pins_pu: uart0-ph-pins-pu {
 	};
 };
 
-/* Prevent cpufreq-dt from binding and crashing with nosmp */
-&cpu0 {
-	/delete-property/ cpu-supply;
-	/delete-property/ operating-points;
-};
-
-
-
 /* AXP221 PMIC is connected via P2WI at 0x68 with NMI interrupt. */
 &battery_power_supply {
 	status = "okay";
-- 
2.56.0

